    "product_id": "9b2e6fb2-522f-4351-9322-b9105ae2aa78",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 261001\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n201 AM PST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Expect breezy north winds along the Colorado River Valley with \n  light winds elsewhere and warming temperatures through the weekend.\n\n* Unsettled weather next week will bring the potential for gusty \n  winds, widespread rainfall, and mountain snow to the region. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Wednesday.\n\nGenerally quiet weather continues across the Desert Southwest for \nThanksgiving Weekend. Expect light winds and sunny skies becoming \npartly cloudy across the forecast area today, with the exception of \nbreezy north winds along the Colorado River Valley through the \nevening. Expect wind gust speeds between 25 and 30 mph near Laughlin \n/ Bullhead City and wave heights to 3 feet on Lake Mohave near \nKatherine Landing as a result. Temperatures will continue to warm \nthrough the weekend, with forecast afternoon highs between 6 and 8 \ndegrees above seasonal normals Friday through Sunday.\n\nConfidence in the forecast for the first half of next week is low at \nthis time. We are watching a weather system that will push into the \nCalifornia Coast as a closed area of low pressure some time between \nTuesday and Wednesday, though both the timing and location of this \nsystem have varied widely over the last couple of days. This system \nwill bring chances for strong gusty winds, widespread rain, and \nmountain snow, though these parameters are heavily influenced by the \nexact trajectory of the system as it swings through the region. Stay \ntuned to the forecast over the next few days as confidence in the \ndetails continue to increase.\n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Winds \nremain light and follow typical, daily patterns. Chance of seeing \n10+ knots is below 10% throughout the TAF period. A few high clouds \ntoday, increasing overnight.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light and diurnal wind \npatterns anticipated across most of the region today and tonight. \nThe exception is the lower Colorado River Valley where northerly \nwinds are likely (80%) to gust 15-30 knots. Highs clouds spread \nacross the area, with the greatest coverage in our northwestern \nlocations. Bases remain above 15kft.\n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Woods\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
